Once you sign, the agreement shows "Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars" under Signed. CarmaCars''s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.

> Good to know: The agreement is signed here, with the e-signature (never on paper).


## How the business is growing

Your Home shows the business''s traction: monthly active users of the website and of the app, and the days rented each month, with the change on the month before and the last 12 months. The figures come from the site''s own records and fill in by themselves.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Home shows what needs you first (a document to sign, a notice, a return on hold), then each of your investments: what you put in, what it earns, and when it pays.</p><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-read-an-investment" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read an investment</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The menu: <b class="gd-ui">Home</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Live sheets</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> (with the tabs <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents to sign</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Your files</b>), <b class="gd-ui">Investor deck</b> (while CarmaCars shares it) and <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Guide</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Sign out</b> are at the top.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your agreement number and name, your Invested Amount, the Returns paid to date (or reinvested) and the next payment, with a chart of your account month by month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each investment: its Invested Amount, how far the lockup period has run, the Yearly Percentage, how Returns are handled (Paid monthly or Reinvested) and the Next Payment Date. Principal, what was reinvested and redeemed to date, the Investment Date and the Lockup End Date are under &quot;Principal, dates and amounts to date&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payment schedule: the last Returns on your statements and the next ones. An amount that is not on a statement yet is marked Estimated.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Latest statement, with <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/1605"><img src="/guides/img/investor-01-investments-phone-16342025.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="1605"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.6%;top:15.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.5%;top:34.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.3%;top:72.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.3%;top:95%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>This area shows your records under your Investment Agreement. It is not an offer or a solicitation.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-live-sheets" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live sheets</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Live sheets</b> is the CarmaCars investment workbook on the website, filled in from your own records. It updates itself: when a payment to you is recorded, it shows as Paid on your next visit.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">My investment</b>: your Invested Amount, start date, Yearly Percentage, lockup end, the payouts made so far and the next payout with its date. Below is your schedule: your statements as recorded (Paid, To be paid, On hold, Reinvested), then the months ahead (Projected). Switch <b class="gd-ui">Paid monthly</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reinvested</b> to compare the months ahead; it does not change your choice (that is a request under Account).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Calculator</b>: type an amount (at least the minimum), a start date and a yearly percentage, and choose Paid monthly or Reinvested. You see the monthly payout, when the lockup ends, the first payment, what is paid by months 24 and 36, and the 36-month schedule. It starts from your own numbers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How it works</b>: the terms of the 2026 raise in plain words, as on the investor deck: Option 1, 10 to 15% a year paid monthly as simple interest, and Option 2, a 20 to 25% profit share from the cars the money puts on the road, with Option 1 examples. Final terms are set in your signed agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fund a car</b>: for buying a car and placing it in the owner program. Type the price, the daily rate, the days you expect it rented and the terms of your owner agreement. It starts from the deck&#39;s example ($112 a rented day for 25 days, an illustration, not a forecast); enter the monthly fees from your agreement. You see your monthly payout, the yearly figures, the return on the car and the payout schedule. Add up to three cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b> gives you the same sheets as a spreadsheet with working formulas, with your numbers filled in. <b class="gd-ui">Download as PDF</b> gives your investment, your schedule and how it works on a few pages.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The sheets show only your own records and the investment terms. The months ahead are estimates; your monthly statement is the record.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-sign-your-investment-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign your investment agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">When CarmaCars sends your agreement, it is under Documents, Documents to sign, and first on Home.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b> on Home, or open <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Documents to sign</b>. The top shows what is signed (&quot;0 of 1 signed&quot;).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values: your name and address, the Invested Amount, the Yearly Percentage and the dates. The agreement is filled in from your record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it, with its schedules.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Say whether you got independent legal advice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the risk acknowledgment (Schedule C), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is on the same page.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Once you sign, the agreement shows &quot;Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars&quot; under Signed. CarmaCars&#39;s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The agreement is signed here, with the e-signature (never on paper).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-how-the-business-is-growing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How the business is growing</h2><p class="gd-p">Your Home shows the business&#39;s traction: monthly active users of the website and of the app, and the days rented each month, with the change on the month before and the last 12 months. The figures come from the site&#39;s own records and fill in by themselves.</p></section>');
